---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';import ToolCard from '../components/ToolCard.astro';import {getCollection} from 'astro:content';
const tools=(await getCollection('tools')).sort((a,b)=>a.data.order-b.data.order);
---
<Base title="Userscripts" description="Practical enhancements for TradingView in a desktop browser, plus Trade Nation shortcuts and trading statistics.">
<section class="section-shell page-intro"><div class="eyebrow">USERSCRIPTS / YOUR BROWSER WORKSPACE</div><h1>Small additions.<br/><span>Less repetition.</span></h1><p class="lead">Make tabs, tickers and watchlists work the way you use them. Add manual broker shortcuts or keep a trading archive.</p><div class="jump-links"><a href="#tradingview">TradingView (browser) ↘</a><a href="#trade-nation">Trade Nation ↘</a><a href="/install/">Installation guide ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="section-shell"><div class="notice"><span class="notice-icon" aria-hidden="true">i</span><div><strong>A desktop browser and a userscript manager.</strong><p>Read the documentation on any device; install and use these tools on desktop. The TradingView tools enhance the website in your browser. They are not Pine indicators and do not run inside the native TradingView Desktop app. Edge or Chrome with Tampermonkey is the current workflow; check each tool's documented setup.</p></div></div></section>
<section id="tradingview" class="section-shell section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">01 / TRADINGVIEW (BROWSER)</div><h2>Make the everyday bits easier.</h2></div><a href="/about/#browser" class="text-link">Why I use a dedicated browser ↗</a></div><div class="tool-grid two">{tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='tradingview').map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div></section>
<section id="trade-nation" class="section-shell section-space border-top"><div class="section-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow">02 / TRADE NATION</div><h2>Act deliberately.<br/>Review the details.</h2></div><p>Manual chart shortcuts and a local history archive. Statistics imports Trade Nation CFD and Spread USD accounts. IG import is not implemented.</p></div><div class="tool-grid two">{tools.filter(t=>t.data.group==='broker').map(tool=><ToolCard tool={tool}/>)}</div></section>
</Base>
